CODEGEN.md §5.13, §5.6: a go types-mode decoder writes an absent key's constant default, and a dependent value's branch is decided by the discriminant it reads, so a dependent field with a present default is DependentDefault at the field (as cpp and ts); none, or an empty list, is written.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// A kind.
enum K { one, two }

/// A payload.
type P(k: K) = match k { one => Int, two => String }

/// A rule.
record Rule {
  /// Its kind.
  k: K
  /// Its payload.
  p: P(k) = 3
  /// An optional payload.
  q: P(k)?
  /// Payloads.
  r: [P(k)] = []
}

emit go { out: "@features/a", package: "a", mode: types }
-- findings.txt --
error[E8019]  a/a.canon:14:3
  emit go in types mode cannot generate a default holding a dependent value, read by a decoder; drop the default, or make the field optional

